### Important streaming distinction

We established that the Hermes CLI emits genuine `type: "text"` chunks. We also verified that adapter callbacks, event storage, and WebSocket code are connected.

An earlier end-to-end test returned zero `hermes.text` events, but that was before the running backend's restart status was resolved. A later successful end-to-end capture has not been supplied.

Therefore, the correct status is unverified end-to-end, rather than definitively broken or working.

### Execution controls

Real Pause, Resume, Stop, and Redirect functionality remains a major missing capability.

This requires process lifecycle management inside the runtime adapter, cancellation propagation across SSH, and a defined restart/recovery policy. A UI button without actual process control would not meet the requirement.

